  "description": "Interested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers, or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\r\n\r\n\r\nSherry Fitzgerald Brady O'Flaherty are pleased to introduce 47, Abbeyfield to the market - Commanding a prime corner position and presented in superlative condition throughout, \r\n\r\n\r\nThis magnificent, energy efficient  3 / 4 bedroom semi-detached residence  extending to 117 sq. m. / 1152 sq. ft. offers a superb blend of space, style and modern convenience. This property has been comprehensively upgraded to an exceptional standard, including new double-glazed windows & doors, flooring, bespoke cabinetry, a beautifully appointed contemporary kitchen and stylish new bathrooms. \r\n\r\nCombining generous family accommodation with high-quality modern finishes this wonderful home is sure to appeal to discerning buyers seeking a spacious and beautifully presented property. Flooded with natural light thanks to its enviable orientation, this outstanding home offers beautifully proportioned accommodation for all the family to enjoy. Accommodation includes;  welcoming hall with guest WC, living room, expansive open plan kitchen / dining room, utility, ground floor bedroom / family room, while on the first floor there 3 further bedrooms(1 ensuite) and the family bathroom. \r\n\r\n\r\nThe generous sized rear garden provides a private, secure and beautiful landscaped, low maintenance setting, ideal for children to play while also offering excellent space for outdoor entertainment and the perfect backdrop for summer barbecues, al fresco dining or simply relaxing in peaceful surroundings. Ample off street parking to front. \r\n\r\n\r\nOccupying a large corner plot in a quite traffic free cul sac. Abbeyfield is a highly desirable family orientated development of just 80 family homes with extensive mature landscaped open spaces, ideally located close to Kilcock town centre and benefiting from direct access to the M4 motorway and the capital. The vibrant university town of Maynooth is less than 10 minutes away by car. \r\n\r\nThe convenience of the location of Abbeyfield cannot be overstated with all amenities on your doorstep including, shops, schools, bus stops, greenway and rail station.\r\n\r\n\r\nCombining an exceptional standard of finish, superb natural light, energy efficiency,  generous gardens and one of Kilcock’s most desirable residential locations, 47, Abbeyfield represents a rare opportunity to acquire a turnkey family home of outstanding quality that is ready for immediate occupation.\n\nEntrance Hallway 1.77m x 4.82m. With tiled flooring, bespoke wall panelling. Guest WC & understairs storage.\n\nLiving Room 3.38m x 5.21m. Nicely appointed room with attractive feature fireplace incorporating solid fuel stove. Bespoke panelling and cabinetry either side of fireplace. Wood effect tiled flooring. Archway to;\n\nKitchen / Dining Area 2.60m x 5.72m. Expansive open plan ‘L’ shaped room with an impressive high gloss contemporary fitted kitchen with ample units. Appliances included in sale. Double doors onto rear garden. Tiled floor.   Dining Area:  2.63m x 3.16m\n\nUtility Room 2.29m x 3.16m. With fitted presses, sink unit, plumbed for WM & dryer.\n\nBedroom 4 / Family Room 2.29m x 4.56m. With wood effect tiled flooring and wall to wall married slide robes.\n\nFirst Floor\n\nPrimary Bedroom 3.23m x 4.28m. With fitted wardrobes. Ensuite 2.34m x 1.17m with shower enclosure, WC & WHB. Fully tiled.\n\nBedroom 2 3.50m x 3.16m. With extensive fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 2.27m x 2.29m. With fitted wardrobes.\n\nBathroom 1.65m x 2.07m. Fully upgraded with large walk-in shower enclosure, WC & WHB. Quality tiling. Triton electric shower.\n\nOutisde To the front, there is ample off-street parking, providing convenient and easily accessible parking for residents and visitors alike.\r\nA 2-metre-wide gated side entrance provides excellent access to the rear garden, making it particularly practical for moving garden equipment, bicycles and other larger items. \r\nThe private, low-maintenance rear garden has been designed with ease of upkeep in mind  The garden features an extensive porcelain-paved patio terrace,  dedicated barbecue stand and built-in seating area further enhance the space and  the 6m x 3m aluminum shed is deal for storing garden equirpment etc.",
